# Line endings are load-bearing for the launcher.
#
# A .command with CRLF fails on macOS with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M",
# which is a confusing way to learn about line endings in an AV booth.

*.command  text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf

# The viewer pages carry inline scripts whose Content-Security-Policy hash the
# relay computes from the file. The hash is line-ending independent (see
# relay/server.py _script_hash), but a CRLF checkout still differs
# byte-for-byte from what everyone else runs; pin them to LF too.
*.html     text eol=lf
